The symmetry energy $S_E$ characterizes how the energy rises as one 
moves away from equal numbers of neutrons and protons,
\begin{equation}
S_E = \frac{1}{8} \frac{\partial^2}{{\partial Y_p}^2} 
\frac{E}{A} \: \biggr|_{Y_p=1/2} \,.
\label{se}
\end{equation}
